{"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament\/kirnbergerii"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kirnbergerII","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Two fifths — D→A and A→E — are each narrowed by ½ of the syntonic comma, equal to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"√(20\/9) ≈ 691.202 cents. One fifth — F♯→C♯ — is narrowed by one schisma","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(32805:32768), equal to 16384:10935 ≈ 699.977 cents. The remaining nine fifths are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pure (3:2). The circle closes exactly because one syntonic comma times one schisma","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"equals one Pythagorean comma.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The two half-comma fifths are unusually flat, giving C-adjacent keys very pure","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"thirds while keys with many sharps or flats suffer greatly.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament\/kirnbergerII"},"met